ivltests/sv_ref_arg_object_fork_detach.v:221: warning: ref formal `out_q' has queue type, so it is bound by VALUE-COPY, not by reference (IEEE 1800-2017 13.5.2 requires a `ref' argument to be a reference to the actual) -- the reads/writes this shape needs go through a type-specific functor the reference-binding path does not implement. This task contains a detached fork (join_none/join_any): a write to `out_q' from a branch that is still running when this task itself returns is LOST, silently -- the copy-out back to the caller's actual runs at the task's own join, before such a branch gets to execute.
